@format 1
@id project.delete-scene
@title Delete named scene
@area 7. Project persistence
@entry input
@summary Remove a named scene through its dropdown-row action while preserving the current window layout.
@section II. Functionality
@flow TB
@related project.save-scene, project.load-scene, project.import-scene, project.export-scene

@alias console = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PConsole
@alias scene = Cadroue.Infrastructure.LScene

[input] Scene delete requested <input>
- Receive the minus-button click from a named scene row and suppress scene loading for that click @ console.PConsoleDeleteHandle(...)
> remove

[remove] Remove saved scene <decision>
- Find the named scene case-insensitively, remove it, and persist the remaining collection @ scene.LSceneDelete(...)
? "Scene not found" > unchanged
? "Scene deleted" > active

[active] Was the deleted scene active? <decision>
- Compare the deleted name with the active scene association @ console.PConsoleDeleteHandle(...)
? "No" > rebuild
? "Yes" > detach

[detach] Clear active association <process>
- Clear the console scene name and the shared active-scene name without applying another scene @ console.PConsoleDeleteHandle(...)
> rebuild

[rebuild] Refresh scene selector <process>
- Rebuild the dropdown items, restore the surviving active selection and checkmark, and update the displayed name @ console.PConsoleSceneRebuild(...)
> result

[result] Scene deleted <output>
= The named scene is absent from persistent storage and the dropdown while the current window layout remains unchanged.

[unchanged] Scene unchanged <output>
= No stored scene matched the requested name, so the selector and active association remain unchanged.
